{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"aventurine-sharpcut-vampirebat","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nMaintained guidance conflates generic HMAC manifest signatures with current plan-review and completion-verifier operation certificates. ADR 0044 defines the DSSE and SSHSIG substrate. ADR 0049 defines asymmetric, environment-attributed operation certificates and legacy compatibility.\n\n## Plan\n- Classify each maintained HMAC statement by its implemented consumer.\n- Describe plan-review and completion-verifier certificates as DSSE envelopes signed through SSHSIG with Ed25519 keys.\n- State that legacy HMAC records remain readable but do not certify these gated operations.\n- Preserve accurate generic HMAC API and manifest-signing guidance for other consumers.\n- Preserve historical migration statements.\n- Exclude `src/rebar/_cli/help/sign.txt` and `docs/llm-framework.md`, which are not stale surfaces.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Current gate guidance describes the asymmetric operation-certificate mechanism.\n- [ ] Generic HMAC utilities remain documented where they are implemented.\n- [ ] Legacy compatibility does not read as current gate certification.\n- [ ] ADR and migration history remains intact.\n- [ ] Signing-related documentation consistency tests and targeted documentation checks pass.\n- [ ] Excluded accurate surfaces remain unchanged.","id":"89af-b080-1216-4229","parent_id":"f7e4-4d33-f231-4774","priority":1,"tags":["documentation","f09","security"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"F09 align operation-certificate guidance with asymmetric signing"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787417206852198001,"uuid":"24b22468-accb-43e3-8d0f-2d72e7ccd05c"}